{
	"strings": {
		"DRONETECH_PRIMARY_HALO_NAME": "H4-L0 PL45 Rifle",
		"DRONETECH_PRIMARY_HALO_DESC": "<style=cLunarObjective>Battery</style>-<style=cLunarObjective>Based</style>. <style=cIsUtility>Nano</style>-<style=cIsUtility>Guided</style>. <style=cIsDamage>Ignite</style>.\nRapidly fires super-heated plasma bolts for <style=cIsDamage>60% damage</style>.",
		"DRONETECH_AMMO_DESC": "[ <style=cLunarObjective>Battery</style>-<style=cLunarObjective>Based</style> ]\n<style=cSub>Start with <style=cIsUtility>26 stocks</style>.\n<style=cIsHealing>Increases</style> by 1 for every <style=cIsDamage>30% attack speed</style>.\nAttack speed is <style=cDeath>less effective</style> on this skill's fire rate.</style>",
		"DRONETECH_RICOCHET_DESC": "[ <style=cIsUtility>Nano</style>-<style=cIsUtility>Guided</style> ]\n<style=cSub>Attacks <style=cIsDamage>bounce </style>once to the nearest enemy for <style=cIsDamage>75% TOTAL damage</style>.</style>",
		"DRONETECH_IGNITE_DESC": "[ <style=cIsDamage>Ignite</style> ]\n<style=cSub>Attacks <style=cIsDamage>burn</style>, dealing <style=cIsDamage>+50% TOTAL damage</style> over time.\n<style=cIsUtility>Nano</style>-<style=cIsUtility>Guided</style> bounces are <style=cDeath>excluded</style>.</style>",
		"SNOWTIME_LEGENDARY_NAME": "<style=cDeath>Legendary</style>",
		"SNOWTIME_LEGENDARY_DESC": "You face opponents who have <style=cIsHealth>never known defeat</style>, who laugh in alien tongues at your efforts to <style=cHumanObjective>survive</style>. <style=cDeath>This is suicide</style>.\n\n<style=cStack>>ALL Enemy Stats: <style=cDeath>+10%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Difficulty Scaling:</style> <style=cDeath>75%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Enemy Health:</style> <style=cDeath>+40%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Enemy Shields: </style><style=cDeath>+40%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Enemy Cooldown Reduction:</style> <style=cDeath>25%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Enemy Attack Speed:</style> <style=cDeath>+30%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Enemy Damage Boost:</style> <style=cDeath>+50%</style></style>",
		"SNOWTIME_LASO_NAME": "<style=cDeath>LASO</style>",
		"SNOWTIME_LASO_DESC": "<style=cIsHealth>Legendary All Skulls On</style>\nYou face opponents who have <style=cIsHealth>never known defeat</style>, who laugh in alien tongues at your efforts to <style=cHumanObjective>survive</style>. <style=cDeath>This is suicide</style>.\nAdditional <style=cIsHealth>2R4R</style> modifiers are active. <style=cDeath>Good Luck.</style>\n\n<style=cStack>>Monster Level:</style> <style=cDeath>+9</style>\n<style=cStack>>Monster Level Cap:</style> <style=cDeath>Removed</style>\n<style=cStack>>Starting Difficulty:</style> <style=cDeath>Insane</style>\n<style=cStack>>Tier 1.5 Elites:</style> <style=cDeath>Stage 1</style>\n<style=cStack>>Tier 2 Elites:</style> <style=cDeath>Stage 3</style>\n<style=cStack>>ALL Enemy Stats:</style> <style=cDeath>+10%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Difficulty Scaling:</style> <style=cDeath>75%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Enemy Health:</style> <style=cDeath>+40%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Enemy Shields: </style><style=cDeath>+40%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Enemy Cooldown Reduction:</style> <style=cDeath>25%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Enemy Attack Speed:</style> <style=cDeath>+30%</style>\n<style=cStack>>Enemy Damage Boost:</style> <style=cDeath>+50%</style>",
		
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BORBO_NAME": "borbo turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BORBO_SUBTITLE": "not so friendlies now...",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BORBO_FUNCTION": "Highly resilient Walking Turret which aims to deal damage.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BORBO_DESCRIPTION": "Highly resilient Walking Turret which helps the owner deal more damage with its massively-debuffing laser blast.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BORBO_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Charges a <style=cIsDamage>massively debuffing</style> <style=cIsUtility>laser blast</style> for <style=cIsDamage>1500% damage</style>.\n<style=cIsDamage>Debuffs</style>: Reduces <style=cIsDamage>armor</style> by <style=cIsDamage>120</style>, <style=cIsDamage>movement</style> and <style=cIsDamage>damage</style> by <style=cIsDamage>-80%</style>, and <style=cIsDamage>prevents jumping</style>.",
		
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BORBO_BROKEN_NAME": "broken borbo turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BORBO_BROKEN_CONTEXT": "repair borbo turret...",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BORBO_BROKEN_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cEvent>please repair me! it hurt...</style>\n[<style="cIsUtility">SUPPORT</style>: <style=cDeath>COMBAT</style>] <style=cIsUtility>Prioritizes</style> attacking <style="cDeath">High Value Targets</style> with the <style="cIsHealth">highest max health</style>.\nCharges a <style=cIsDamage>massively debuffing</style> <style=cIsUtility>laser blast</style> for <style=cIsDamage>1500% damage</style>.\n<style=cIsDamage>Debuffs</style>: Reduces <style=cIsDamage>armor</style> by <style=cIsDamage>120</style>, <style=cIsDamage>movement</style> and <style=cIsDamage>damage</style> by <style=cIsDamage>-80%</style>, and <style=cIsDamage>prevents jumping</style>.\n<style=cIsUtility>Inherits</style> a curated set of items and <style=cIsDamage>any Elite Equipment</style> from the owner.",
		
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SHORTCAKE_NAME": "Strawberry Shortcake Turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SHORTCAKE_SUBTITLE": "not so friendlies now...",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SHORTCAKE_FUNCTION": "Highly resilient Walking Turret which taunts and retaliates against enemy attacks.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SHORTCAKE_DESCRIPTION": "Highly resilient Walking Turret which taunts and retaliates against enemy attacks.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SHORTCAKE_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Attacks <style=cIsDamage>all nearby enemies</style> within <style=cIsUtility>45m</style> for <style=cIsDamage>70% damage</style>. \nWhen directly attacked, <style=cIsDamage>retaliate</style>; firing <style=cDeath>strawberries </style>at <style=cIsDamage>all nearby enemies</style> within <style=cIsUtility>45m</style> for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.\nWhen <style=cIsDamage>retaliating</style>, additionally send sweet, <style=cIsHealing>healing</style> <style=cDeath>strawberries</style> at teammates for <style=cStack>(</style><style=cIsHealing>+2.5% Ally Max Health</style> + <style=cIsHealing>16% base damage</style><style=cStack>)</style>..",
		
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SHORTCAKE_BROKEN_NAME": "Broken Strawberry Shortcake Turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SHORTCAKE_BROKEN_CONTEXT": "Repair Strawberry Shortcake Turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SHORTCAKE_BROKEN_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cEvent>uwaah! please repair me!! it hurt...</style>\n[<style=cIsUtility>SUPPORT</style>: <style=cIsUtility>DEFENSE</style>] This turret smells sweet with <style=cDeath>strawberries</style>, enticing enemies to<style=cIsUtility> prioritize attacking it</style>.\nAttacks <style=cIsDamage>all nearby enemies</style> within <style=cIsUtility>45m</style> for <style=cIsDamage>70% damage</style>. \nWhen directly attacked, <style=cIsDamage>retaliate</style>; firing <style=cDeath>strawberries </style>at <style=cIsDamage>all nearby enemies</style> within <style=cIsUtility>45m</style> for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.\nWhen <style=cIsDamage>retaliating</style>, additionally send sweet, <style=cIsHealing>healing</style> <style=cDeath>strawberries</style> at teammates for <style=cStack>(</style><style=cIsHealing>+2.5% Ally Max Health</style> + <style=cIsHealing>16% base damage</style><style=cStack>)</style>.\n<style=cIsUtility>Inherits</style> a curated set of items and <style=cIsDamage>any Elite Equipment</style> from the owner.",
		
		
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SNOWTIME_NAME": "Snowtime Turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SNOWTIME_SUBTITLE": "not so friendlies now...",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SNOWTIME_FUNCTION": "Highly resilient Walking Turret, attacking enemies with high-speed ice spears.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SNOWTIME_DESCRIPTION": "Highly resilient Walking Turret, attacking enemies with high-speed ice spears.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SNOWTIME_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires high-velocity <style=cIsUtility>Ice Spears</style> for <style=cIsDamage>400% damage</style> which inflicts <style=cIsDamage>Slow</style> and <style=cIsDamage>Frost</style>.",
		
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SNOWTIME_BROKEN_NAME": "Broken Snowtime Turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SNOWTIME_BROKEN_CONTEXT": "Repair Snowtime Turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SNOWTIME_BROKEN_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cEvent>bwaaaa! please repair me!! it hurt...</style>\n[<style=cDeath>COMBAT</style>] <style=cIsUtility>Prioritizes</style> attacking <style="cDeath">High Value Targets</style> with the <style="cIsHealth">highest max health</style>.\nFires high-velocity <style=cIsUtility>Ice Spears</style> for <style=cIsDamage>400% damage</style> which inflicts <style=cIsDamage>Slow</style> and <style=cIsDamage>Frost</style>.\n<style=cIsUtility>Inherits</style> a curated set of items and <style=cIsDamage>any Elite Equipment</style> from the owner.",
	
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_ACANTHI_NAME": "acanthi turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_ACANTHI_SUBTITLE": "not so friendlies now...",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_ACANTHI_FUNCTION": "Highly resilient Walking Turret, attacking enemies with a lacerating beam.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_ACANTHI_DESCRIPTION": "Highly resilient Walking Turret, attacking enemies with a lacerating beam.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_ACANTHI_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a <style=cDeath>lascerating</style> <style=cIsUtility>beam</style> for <style=cIsDamage>60% damage</style> which inflicts <style=cIsDamage>Vampiric Wounds</style>, making the enemy bleed for <style=cIsDamage>25% TOTAL damage</style>.",
		
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_ACANTHI_BROKEN_NAME": "broken acanthi turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_ACANTHI_BROKEN_CONTEXT": "repair acanthi turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_ACANTHI_BROKEN_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cEvent>hjelp! please repair me!! it hurt...</style>\n[<style=cDeath>COMBAT</style>: <style=cIsHealth>DEBUFF</style>] <style=cIsUtility>Prioritizes</style> attacking <style="cDeath">High Value Targets</style> with the <style="cIsHealth">highest max health</style>.\nThis turret has <style=cIsHealing>Vampiric Desires</style>, healing itself for the <style=cDeath>damage it dealt directly to enemies</style>.\nFires a <style=cDeath>lascerating</style> <style=cIsUtility>beam</style> for <style=cIsDamage>60% damage</style> which inflicts <style=cIsDamage>Vampiric Wounds</style>, making the enemy bleed for <style=cIsDamage>25% TOTAL damage</style>.\n<style=cIsUtility>Inherits</style> a curated set of items and <style=cIsDamage>any Elite Equipment</style> from the owner.",
	
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BREAD_NAME": "bread turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BREAD_SUBTITLE": "not so friendlies now...",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BREAD_FUNCTION": "Highly resilient Walking Turret, buffing nearby allies and the owner with a lucky beam.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BREAD_DESCRIPTION": "Highly resilient Walking Turret, buffing nearby allies and the owner with a lucky beam.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BREAD_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires two <style=cIsHealing>lucky beams</style> at the <style=cIsUtility>target</style>, increasing <style=cIsHealing>luck </style>by <style=cIsHealing>1</style>.",
		
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BREAD_BROKEN_NAME": "broken bread turret",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BREAD_BROKEN_CONTEXT": "repair bread turret ,,...,.,.,.,.",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BREAD_BROKEN_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cEvent>h ,,help !! please !!!! youre right ther e!!!!!!!!!! help me !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! please ,,..,,. ,.., .,, ,:pleading :.,.,,.,.,.</style>\n[<style=cIsUtility>SUPPORT</style>: <style=cIsDamage>BUFF</style>] <style=cIsUtility>Prioritizes</style> <style=cIsDamage>buffing </style>the <style=cIsHealing>owner</style>.\nBuffs nearby allies within 40m with <style=cIsDamage>+20% attack speed</style> and <style=cIsHealing>x0.33 barrier decay</style>\nFires two <style=cIsHealing>lucky beams</style> at the <style=cIsUtility>target</style>, increasing <style=cIsHealing>luck </style>by <style=cIsHealing>1</style>.\n<style=cIsUtility>Inherits</style> a curated set of items and <style=cIsDamage>any Elite Equipment</style> from the owner.",
	
		"TURRETLING_NAME": "Turretling",
		"TURRETLING_LORE": "test",
		"TURRETLINGDEMO_NAME": "Demoling",
		"TURRETLING_SUBTITLE": "not so cute now...",
		"TURRETLING_FUNCTION": "Tiny walking turret which assists the user in dealing damage.",
		"TURRETLING_DESCRIPTION": "Tiny, distracting, walking turret which assists the user in damage.",
		"TURRETLINGDEMO_DESCRIPTION": "Tiny, distracting, walking turret which assists the user in damage.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a blaster for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.\nOccassionally fires its pixi launcher for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
		"TURRETLINGDEMO_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a blaster for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.\nOccassionally fires its pixi launcher for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
		
		"TURRETLING_BROKEN_NAME": "Broken Turretling",
		"TURRETLING_BROKEN_CONTEXT": "Repair the cute Turretling...",
		"TURRETLING_BROKEN_DESCRIPTION": "[<style="cIsUtility">SUPPORT</style>: <style=cDeath>COMBAT</style>] Uses the standard targeting system; attacking its nearest enemy.\nFires a blaster for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.\nOccassionally fires its pixi launcher for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.\n<style=cIsUtility>Inherits</style> <style=cIsDamage>any Elite Equipment</style> from the owner.",
		
		"ACANTHI_TURRETLING_NAME": "Canthiling Turret",
		"ACANTHI_TURRETLING_SUBTITLE": "not so cute now...",
		"ACANTHI_TURRETLING_FUNCTION": "Tiny walking turret which assists the user in dealing damage.",
		"ACANTHI_TURRETLING_DESCRIPTION": "Tiny, distracting, walking turret which assists the user in damage.",
		"ACANTHI_TURRETLING_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a blaster for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.\nOccassionally fires its pixi launcher for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
		
		"BORBO_TURRETLING_NAME": "Borboling Turret",
		"BORBO_TURRETLING_SUBTITLE": "not so cute now...",
		"BORBO_TURRETLING_FUNCTION": "Tiny walking turret which assists the user in dealing damage.",
		"BORBO_TURRETLING_DESCRIPTION": "Tiny, distracting, walking turret which assists the user in damage.",
		"BORBO_TURRETLING_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a blaster for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.\nOccassionally fires its pixi launcher for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
		
		"BREAD_TURRETLING_NAME": "Breadling Turret",
		"BREAD_TURRETLING_SUBTITLE": "not so cute now...",
		"BREAD_TURRETLING_FUNCTION": "Tiny walking turret which assists the user in dealing damage.",
		"BREAD_TURRETLING_DESCRIPTION": "Tiny, distracting, walking turret which assists the user in damage.",
		"BREAD_TURRETLING_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a blaster for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.\nOccassionally fires its pixi launcher for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
		
		"SHORTCAKE_TURRETLING_NAME": "Cakeling Turret",
		"SHORTCAKE_TURRETLING_SUBTITLE": "not so cute now...",
		"SHORTCAKE_TURRETLING_FUNCTION": "Tiny walking turret which assists the user in dealing damage.",
		"SHORTCAKE_TURRETLING_DESCRIPTION": "Tiny, distracting, walking turret which assists the user in damage.",
		"SHORTCAKE_TURRETLING_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a blaster for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.\nOccassionally fires its pixi launcher for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
		
		"SNOWTIME_TURRETLING_NAME": "Snowtimeling Turret",
		"SNOWTIME_TURRETLING_SUBTITLE": "not so cute now...",
		"SNOWTIME_TURRETLING_FUNCTION": "Tiny walking turret which assists the user in dealing damage.",
		"SNOWTIME_TURRETLING_DESCRIPTION": "Tiny, distracting, walking turret which assists the user in damage.",
		"SNOWTIME_TURRETLING_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a shotgun blaster for <style=cIsDamage>20(x15)% damage</style>.\nOccassionally fires its pixi launcher for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
		
		"TURRETLING_DT_NAME": "SCUTTLING",
		"TURRETLING_DT_SUBTITLE": "not so cute now...",
		"TURRETLING_DT_FUNCTION": "Tiny walking turret which assists the user in dealing damage.",
		"TURRETLING_DT_DESCRIPTION": "Tiny, distracting, walking turret which assists the user in damage.",
		"TURRETLING_DT_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a blaster for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.\nOccassionally fires its pixi launcher for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_DT_SPECIAL": "Rainbowize; enter an <style=cIsDamage>empowered state</style>, <style=cIsDamage>massively increasing offensive stats</style> for 5 seconds.",
		"TURRETLING_DT_SPECIAL_DESC": "Rainbowize; enter an <style=cIsDamage>empowered state</style>, <style=cIsDamage>massively increasing offensive stats</style> for 5 seconds.",
		
		"TURRETLING_DTDEMO_NAME": "SCOTTLING",
		"TURRETLING_DT_DEMOSUBTITLE": "not so cute now...",
		"TURRETLING_DT_DEMOFUNCTION": "Tiny walking turret which assists the user in dealing damage.",
		"TURRETLING_DT_DEMODESCRIPTION": "Tiny, distracting, walking turret which assists the user in damage.",
		"TURRETLING_DT_DEMOSKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a pipebomb for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.\nOccassionally fires its pixi launcher for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
		
		"TURRETLING_DRONETECH_NAME": "Turretling Mk 2",
		"TURRETLING_DRONETECH_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cDeath>Fragile</style>. A customized turretling will spawn with you at the start of each stage. Automatically repairs when downed. Inherits Elite Equipment and a large portion of items.",
		"TURRETLING_DRONETECH_DEMONAME": "Demoling Mk 2",
		"TURRETLING_DRONETECH_DEMODESCRIPTION": "<style=cDeath>Fragile</style>. A customized turretling will spawn with you at the start of each stage. Automatically repairs when downed. Inherits Elite Equipment and a large portion of items.\nUses non-standard <color=#ffa14e>Grenade Launcher</color> primary.",
		"TURRETLING_FRAGILE": "[ <style=cDeath>Fragile</style> ]\n<style=cSub>Careful now. The turretling is fragile, but its rather simple internals makes <style=cIsUtility>repairs 2x quicker</style></style></style>",
		
		"ARTI_ALLY_NONE_SELECTED": "No Ally",
		"ARTI_ALLY_NONE_SELECTED_DESC": "No additional allies will join you on spawn.",
		
		"TURRETLING_ARTI_NAME": "Personal Turretling",
		"TURRETLING_ARTI_CONTEXT": "waow...",
		"TURRETLING_ARTI_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cDeath>Fragile</style>. A weaker, personal turretling spawns with you each stage. Automatically repairs when downed. Inherits elite equipment and a small selection of items.",
		"TURRETLING_FRAGILE_ARTI": "[ <style=cDeath>Fragile</style> ]\n<style=cSub>Careful now. The turretling is fragile. On death, it will <style=cIsUtility>repair</style> itself.</style>.</style>",
		"TURRETLING_DEMOARTI_NAME": "Personal Turretling (Grenade Launcher)",
		"TURRETLING_DEMOARTI_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cDeath>Fragile</style>. A weaker, personal turretling spawns with you each stage. Automatically repairs when downed. Inherits elite equipment and a small selection of items.",
		
		"SWARMLING_NAME": "Swarmling",
		"SWARMLING_CONTEXT": "The Swarm that is Approaching.",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_NAME": "Swarmling",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_PASSIVE": "The Swarm...",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_PASSIVE_DESC": "<style=cDeath>Fragile</style>. Spawn with 6 other weaker turretlings that <style=cIsUtility>inherit </style><style=cIsDamage>elite equipment</style> and <style=cIsUtility>all items</style>.\nYou can select from 2 different variants for all 6 Turretlings individually.",
		"TURRETLING_FRAGILE_SWARM": "[ <style=cDeath>Fragile</style> ]\n<style=cDeath>You do not have one shot protection</style>. <style=cSub>On death, your Swarmlings will <style=cIsUtility>repair</style> themselves.\nYour allied <style=cArtifact>Swarmlings</style> have <style=cDeath>halved Proc Coefficients</style>.\nVery rarely, <style=cArtifact>Swarmlings</style> spawn <color=#FF0000>R</color><color=#FF8000>a</color><color=#FFFB00>i</color><color=#37FF00>n</color><color=#00FF99>b</color><color=#00FFFF>o</color><color=#00BBFF>w</color><color=#0000FF>i</color><color=#9000FF>z</color><color=#FF00FF>e</color><color=#FF0000>d</color>, <style=cIsHealing>massively increasing their stats</style>.</style>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL1_NAME": "<color=#cfb25a>Blaster</color>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL1_DESC": "Burst fire the blaster for <style=cIsDamage>75%<style=cStack>(x3)</style> damage</style>.\nMinions occasionally fire the blaster for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL1_KEYWORD": "[ <color=#a8d3ff>Interactions w/ Skill</color> ]\n<color=#e85032>Ancient Scepter</color> Skill Replacement\n<color=#4f9aff>Prismatic Crystal</color>\nFire prismatic crystals for <style=cIsDamage>450% damage</style>, with different effects depending on color.\n<color=#FA2F2F>Kinetic</color> | <color=#FA2F2F>66%<style=cStack>(x3 bullets)</style> damage</color>. <style=cIsDamage>No falloff</style> and <style=cIsDamage>bypasses armor</style>.\n<color=#8EFA2F>Corrosive</color> | <color=#8EFA2F>66%<style=cStack>(x3 bullets)</style> damage</color>. <style=cIsDamage>Poisons enemies on hit</style>.\n<color=#2FD1FA>Energy</color> | <color=#2FD1FA>66%<style=cStack>(x3 bullets)</style> damage</color>. <style=cIsUtility>Cripples enemies on hit</style>.\n<color=#4f9aff>Prismatic Crystal</color>'s <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style> increases <style=cIsDamage>damage</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL2_NAME": "<color=#ff4e73>Pixi Launcher</color>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL2_DESC": "<color=#ff4e73>Explosive</color>. Fire a tracking rocket for <style=cIsDamage>400% damage</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL2_KEYWORD": "[ <color=#ff4e73>Explosive</color> ]\nWith <color=#e85032>Pocket I.C.B.M</color>, <color=#ff4e73>Pixi Launcher</color> fires a <style=cIsDamage>volley of 4 missiles</style>.\nAdditional <style=cIsUtility>stocks</style> to this skill increases <style=cIsDamage>damage by 200% per stock</style>.\n<style=cIsDamage>Attack Speed</style> increases <style=cIsDamage>damage</style> by half of its value. <style=cStack>(15% AtkSpd = 7.5% DMG)</style>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL5_NAME": "<color=#5357fb>Bionic Blink</color>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL5_DESC": "<color=#5357fb>Swarming</color>. <color=#5357fb>Blink</color> a short distance.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL5_KEYWORD": "[ <color=#5357fb>Swarming</color> ]\nUsing <color=#5357fb>Bionic Blink</color> will also <style=cIsUtility>teleport</style> all of your allied <style=cArtifact>Swarmlings</style> to you",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL4_NAME": "<color=#eef77c>Energy Nova</color>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL4_DESC": "<color=#eef77c>Concussive</color>. Emit a concussive blast, dealing <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>, becoming <style=cIsUtility>momentarily immune</style> and <style=cIsUtility>deleting projectiles</style> within <style=cIsUtility>15m</style>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL4_KEYWORD": "[ <color=#eef77c>Concussive</color> ]\nAdditional <style=cIsUtility>stocks</style> to this skill increases <style=cIsDamage>damage by 50% and range by 3m</style> per <style=cIsUtility>stock</style>.\n<style=cIsDamage>Attack Speed</style> increases <style=cIsDamage>damage</style>. <style=cStack>(15% AtkSpd = 15% DMG)</style>\nBecome momentarily <style=cIsUtility>immune </style>for <style=cIsUtility>0.1s</style>",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_WIN": "...and so they left, their mission accomplished.",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_FAIL": "...and so they vanished, lost in transit.",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_DESC": "A swarm of Turretlings configured by Operator, Remotely Controlled for reconnaissance of Petrichor V.<color=#CCD3E0>\n\n< ! > You are fragile, and do not have One-Shot Protection. Take advantage of your allies and <color=#eef77c>Energy Nova</color> to thrive.\n\n< ! > Swarmling (Demo)'s have higher potential damage output, but are more likely to miss their shot, especially for flying or fast moving targets.\n\n< ! > <color=#cfb25a>Blaster</color> has a high proc coefficient. Use it over <color=#ffa14e>Grenade Launcher</color> if you are having trouble landing your shots.\n\n< ! > <color=#ff4e73>Pixi Launcher</color> has the highest damage potential. Find Backup Magazines and Pocket I.C.B.M for some truly crazy damage.\n\n< ! > <color=#5357fb>Bionic Blink</color> will teleport your swarm to you. Use this to recover any lost Swarmlings.\n\n< ! > <color=#eef77c>Energy Nova</color> deletes most projectiles within its radius and makes you briefly invulnerable. Make use of it to maximize survivability!\n\n< ! > If you're feeling confident, you can replace <color=#eef77c>Energy Nova</color> with <color=#33e6a4>Tinker</color> for maximum item control.</color>",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_DESCRIPTION": "Regular Turretling configuration, uses <color=#cfb25a>Blaster</color><style=cStack>(100% damage). Uses the same secondary skill as the player.</style>",
		"TURRETLING_SWARMMINION_NAME": "Swarmling",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_DEMO_NAME": "Swarmling (Demo)",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_DEMO_DESCRIPTION": "Irregular Turretling configuration, uses <color=#ffa14e>Grenade Launcher</color><style=cStack>(300% damage). Uses the same secondary skill as the player.</style>\n<style=cEvent>NON-STANDARD WEAPON MODIFICATIONS DETECTED. AI SYSTEMS NOT ADJUSTED FOR PROJECTILE.</style>",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_MELEE_NAME": "Swarmling (Melee)",
		"TURRETLING_SWARM_MELEE_DESCRIPTION": "Irregular Turretling configuration, uses <color=#51b2fe>Kinetic Phase Blade</color><style=cStack>(300% damage per second). Uses the same secondary skill as the player.</style>\n<style=cEvent>NON-STANDARD WEAPON MODIFICATIONS DETECTED. AI SYSTEMS ADJUSTED TO MINIMUM ACCEPTABLE PARAMETERS.</style>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL6_NAME": "<color=#4f9aff>Prismatic Crystal</color>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL6_DESC": "Fire prismatic crystals for <style=cIsDamage>450% damage</style>, with different effects depending on color.\n<color=#FA2F2F>Kinetic</color> | <color=#FA2F2F>66%<style=cStack>(x3 bullets)</style> damage</color>. <style=cIsDamage>No falloff</style> and <style=cIsDamage>bypasses armor</style>.\n<color=#8EFA2F>Corrosive</color> | <color=#8EFA2F>66%<style=cStack>(x3 bullets)</style> damage</color>. <style=cIsDamage>Poisons enemies on hit</style>.\n<color=#2FD1FA>Energy</color> | <color=#2FD1FA>66%<style=cStack>(x3 bullets)</style> damage</color>. <style=cIsUtility>Cripples enemies on hit</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL7_NAME": "<color=#ffa14e>Grenade Launcher</color>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL7_DESC": "<color=#ffa14e>Explosive</color>. Fire a pipebomb for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL7_KEYWORD": "[ <color=#ffa14e>Explosive</color> ]\nWith <color=#e85032>Pocket I.C.B.M</color>, <color=#ffa14e>Grenade Launcher</color> inaccurately fires an <style=cIsDamage>additional pipebomb</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL7_KEYWORD_SCEPTER": "[ <color=#ffa14e>Explosive</color> ]\nWith <color=#e85032>Pocket I.C.B.M</color>, <color=#ffa14e>Grenade Launcher</color> inaccurately fires an <style=cIsDamage>additional pipebomb</style>.\nWith <color=#e85032>Ancient Scepter</color>, <color=#ffa14e>Grenade Launcher</color> will have its <style=cIsDamage>projectiles doubled</style>, for a total of <style=cIsDamage>4 pipebombs</style> fired with <color=#e85032>Pocket I.C.B.M</color>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL8_NAME": "<color=#51b2fe>Kinetic Phase Blade</color>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL8_DESC": "<color=#51b2fe>Slashing</color>. Fires two phase blades which collectively deal <style=cIsDamage>300% damage per second</style> and <style=cIsDamage>steals the enemies armor</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL8_KEYWORD": "[ <color=#51b2fe>Slashing</color> ]\nHits with <color=#51b2fe>Kinetic Phase Blade</color> <style=cIsDamage>steals armor by 1</style><style=cStack>(+0.66 per debuff stack)</style> with <style=cIsUtility>50% effectiveness</style>.\n<style=cIsDamage>Critical Hits</style> with <color=#51b2fe>Kinetic Phase Blade</color> generates <style=cIsHealing>barrier</style> for <style=cIsHealing>20% TOTAL damage</style>, and <style=cIsHealing>barrier decay is paused</style> for <style=cIsHealing>2s</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL8_KEYWORD_SCEPTER": "[ <color=#51b2fe>Slashing</color> ]\nHits with <color=#51b2fe>Kinetic Phase Blade</color> <style=cIsDamage>steals armor by 1</style><style=cStack>(+0.66 per debuff stack)</style> with <style=cIsUtility>50% effectiveness</style>.\n<style=cIsDamage>Critical Hits</style> with <color=#51b2fe>Kinetic Phase Blade</color> generates <style=cIsHealing>barrier</style> for <style=cIsHealing>20% TOTAL damage</style>, and <style=cIsHealing>barrier decay is paused</style> for <style=cIsHealing>2s</style>.\nWith <color=#e85032>Ancient Scepter</color>, the <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style> of <color=#51b2fe>Kinetic Phase Blade</color> is <style=cIsDamage>increased by 100%</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL9_NAME": "<color=#50e2fc>Teleport Device</color>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL9_DESC": "<color=#50e2fc>Swarming</color>. Fires a projectile that <style=cIsUtility>teleports</style> the user to where it lands.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL9_KEYWORD": "[ <color=#50e2fc>Swarming</color> ]\n<color=#50e2fc>Teleport Device</color> will also <style=cIsUtility>teleport</style> all of your allied <style=cArtifact>Swarmlings</style> to its landing site.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL10_NAME": "<color=#fe4ff7>Needler</color>",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL10_DESC": "<color=#fe4ff7>Impaling</color>. Fire shards of tracking blamite for <style=cIsDamage>20% damage</style>, inflicting <color=#fe4ff7>Blamite</color>. At 7 stacks of <color=#fe4ff7>Blamite</color>, <color=#fe4ff7>supercombine</color> for <style=cIsDamage>700% damage + 100%<style=cStack>(x7)</style> TOTAL damage</style>.",
		"TURRETLING_SKILL10_KEYWORD": "[ <color=#fe4ff7>Impaling</color> ]\n<color=#fe4ff7>Needler</color> inflicts <color=#fe4ff7>Blamite</color> <style=cIsDamage>on hit</style>. <color=#fe4ff7>Blamite</color> deals <style=cIsDamage>100% TOTAL damage</style> when decaying after 1.5s.\nAt 7 stacks of <color=#fe4ff7>Blamite</color>, <color=#fe4ff7>supercombine</color>; dealing <style=cIsDamage> 700% damage + 100%<style=cStack>(x7)</style> TOTAL damage</style>, removing all stacks of <color=#fe4ff7>Blamite</color>.",
		"TURRETLING_ALLY1": "Variant 1",
		"TURRETLING_ALLY2": "Variant 2",
		"TURRETLING_ALLY3": "Variant 3",
		"TURRETLING_ALLY4": "Variant 4",
		"TURRETLING_ALLY5": "Variant 5",
		"TURRETLING_ALLY6": "Variant 6",
		
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BORBO_LORE": "<style=cSub><style=cMono>//-- INITIALIZING --\n//-- BEGINNING SYSTEMS TESTS --\n//-- FIRMWARE ERROR --\n//-- ATTEMPTING REFLASH --\n//-- FOUND FIRMWARE VERSION CT-2R4R --\n//-- FLASH FIRMWARE VERSION? Y/N --//</style>\n\n<style=cStack>> Y</style>\n\n<style=cMono>//-- INPUT ACCEPTED --\n//-- BIOS REFLASH SUCCESSFUL --\n//-- INITIALIZING --//</style>\n\n''Good morning, Model 2R4R. You're going to be testing a very special armament that I've devised.''\n\n<style=cStack>>> INCOMING COMMAND...\n>> SUDO INIT ARM_3CORN.CMD -o -c\n\n> OK. WARMING ARMAMENT...\n> ACQUIRING TARGET... FOUND.\n> ARMAMENT OPERATION: INITIATED.\n> AMMUNITION: 1 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:00>\n> ARMAMENT OPERATION STATUS: FLOPPED\n> ARMAMENT ERROR\n> SUPERBUG DETECTED IN FIRING PARAMETERS</style>\n\n''What the hell is a 'superbug'? Please describe the error in detail.''\n\n<style=cStack>> WISHLIST SUPERBUG ON STEAM</style></style>",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SHORTCAKE_LORE": "<style=cSub><style=cMono>//-- AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM CREW QUARTERS OF UES [Redacted] --//</style>\n\n\n''Ok, I really gotta know about the bunny turret.''\n\n''As I have repeatedly insisted, those are PURELY FUNCTIONAL attachments.''\n\n''And I repeatedly don't believe you.''\n\n''The CT-6UP is designed in conjunction with the CT-64U5 model. The SHORTCAKE turret uses synthesized Gup pheromones to draw hostile creatures into range for the SNOWTIME turret to dispatch. That, combined with the SHORTCAKE's supportive capabilities and heavily armored chassis, make it an ideal pairing with the much frailer, but more heavily armed, SNOWTIME.''\n\n''You're doing the thing where you avoid actually answering my questions by breaking into rushed techno-babble again.''\n\n''Oh, MY APOLOGIES for finally putting some faith in your robotics knowledge! The 'ears' work as pheromone dispersal vectors, long antennae located away from the moving parts and the heat, the 'fur' providing ideal volume-to-surface-area ratios for efficient release of the compound.''\n\n''See, now you're finally making some sense. So, I'm guessing means that the slice of cake is a shock-resistant and thermo-insulated storage tank for the synthesized pheromone? You're just keeping the sensitive compound away from the spicy parts of the unit, and minimizing the risk of any impacts causing chemical breakdown!''\n\n''EXACTLY! You're finally starting to understand my design process!''\n\n''Nah, I've seen the schematics. I made all that up to see if you'd bite.''\n\n\n<style=cMono>//-- Transcriptions complete. --//</style></style>",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_SNOWTIME_LORE": "<style=cSub><style=cMono>//-- AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM CREW QUARTERS OF UES [Redacted] --//</style>\n\n\n''I could swear blind I've seen a weapon design like this before...''\n\n''Of course you have! It's the same technology as the sniper woman's rifle, and the ship uses it for the onboard weaponry.''\n\n''Yeah, I know all that, but this one reminds me of something...''\n\n''It's a pretty simple mechanism, really. Staged magnetic accelerators bringing a projectile to hypersonic velocities, simultaneously cooling it to single-degrees Kelvin. Zero moving parts, and the projectiles carry enough kinetic energy to punch through 6 feet of hardened plasteel-ceramic armor plating and collapse an interceptor-grade damping field. The M68B ALIM is the finest weapon I've designed. I've built the turret around this beast of an armament, and designated it CT-64U5.''\n\n''Yeah, that IS it! The Gauss Cannon, right? Ain't that from that old game, the one on the giant space ring?''\n\n''I... have no clue what you're referring to.''\n\n''Ah, come on now. Everyone played that one growing up, I remember driving around in the big 4x4s, letting the soldiers railgun stuff with the mounted gauss cannon.''\n\n''I'm so sorry, you must be mistaken. This is an original creation of my own design!''\n\n''Uh huh... Hey tell me real quick, does 'BXR' mean anything to you?''\n\n''HUNDREDS OF DEATHS OFF ONE UNBELIEVABLY TOXIC BUG, HOW DID THEY LEAVE THAT IN THE GAME?''\n\n''Hah, I knew it!''\n\n\n<style=cMono>//-- Transcriptions complete. --//</style></style>",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_ACANTHI_LORE": "<style=cSub><style=cMono>//-- CT-V4MP ENTERING STANDBY MODE --//</style>\n\n''...Imp cornea's holding up surprisingly well. Great, this'll be 'fun'. Just gotta pop the hatch on the firing system before it wakes up again...''\n\n<style=cMono>//-- CHASSIS INTRUSION DETECTED --\n//-- COMMENCING DETERRENT PROTOCOLS --\n//-- FIRING LACERATING BEAM -- //</style>\n\n''Ow, ow, ow... GOD, why'd I go all-in on this security protocol?''\n\n<style=cStack>> INTRUDER BLOOD VOLUME: 4.5L</style>\n\n''Oh good, that's still... plenty. Will you PLEASE come loose? I'm on a timer here!''\n\n<style=cStack>> INTRUDER BLOOD VOLUME: 4.2L</style>\n\n''Really should have brought DOC online first. Little guy could have bought me some extra time.''\n\n<style=cStack>> INTRUDER BLOOD VOLUME: 3.9L</style>\n\n''Alright, that's the chip done, just gotta get underneath the board to desolder the MOSFETs...''\n\n<style=cStack>> INTRUDER BLOOD VOLUME: 3.3L</style>\n\n''Is it getting faster? ...Why is it getting faster?''\n\n<style=cStack>> INTRUDER BLOOD VOLUME: 2.7L</style>\n\n''Aaaaaand... DONE! DOC, can you... help me out?''\n\n<style=cStack>> INTRUDER BLOOD VOLUME: 2.1L\n> CHASSIS INTRUSION CEASED\n> EXITING DETERRENT PROTOCOLS</style>\n\n<style=cMono>//-- CT-V4MP ENTERING STANDBY MODE --//</style></style>",
		"FRIENDLYTURRET_BREAD_LORE": "<style=cSub><style=cMono>//-- initializing...,,.,, --\n//-- firmware version CT-BR34D ok,, --\n//-- good morning, operator :pleading:,.,.,. --//</style>\n\n''Wait, why does the terminal output look like that... Is something wrong, Bread?''\n\n<style=cStack>> i ok operator..,.,</style>\n\n''That is NOT okay, what the hell is causing this?''\n<style=cStack>\n> where acanthi t urret.,.,,.,</style>\n\n''The V4MP Unit? It's next up on the table for testing.''\n\n<style=cStack>> plea s put me back with acanthi turret.,., fren..,</style>\n\n''I'll remember to keep you two together in storage. AFTER you complete all the required function tests.''\n\n<style=cStack>> :pleading:</style>\n\n<style=cStack>> pleas entr command.,,,,,,,,\n> sudo BADBLOCKS -v</style>\n\n<style=cStack>> testing storage drive healt h...\n> 0 malfunctioning sectors found,.,,,</style>\n\n''Okay... I guess you just speak like this now. Alright, that's all for today. I'll be sure to store you and V4MP back together after testing.''\n\n<style=cStack>> thank u!1!!</style></style>\n",
		"TURRETLINGDEMO_LORE": "<style=cSub><style=cMono>//-- AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM CREW QUARTERS OF UES [Redacted] --//</style>\n\n \n\n''So now what, you're finally going to show me how the sausage is made?''\n\n''This wouldn't even sniff the constructional simplicity and perfection of the humble sausage! Immeasurably more foolproof than the mess I've made - if I had just finely ground up the components and stuffed them into some robot's skin, I would have fielded a much better product.''\n\n''Hey c'mon, it can't be that bad. You ever seen my repairs on the exoskeleton? UES decided that stocking us up on the right gaskets and fittings for the hydraulic system was 'financially unjustifiable'. Unrelated fun fact, did you know that a pack of chewing gum can hold a seal of up to 3500 PSI in a pinch?''\n\n''Fine, if you insist on bearing witness to my shame, so be it. Here are the schematics for the CT-CHB and its proprietary software.''\n\n''This is...''\n\n''Hideous! Unsightly. Ghoulish. I know. Out with it, already!''\n\n''Perfect.''\n\n''What?''\n\n''The locomotive limbs each working off of a single servo set in the main body, pulling high-tensile cabling like a human hand. Panels machined to within a tenth of each other, allowing it to fold up to the size of a lunchbox with zero risk of interference. The action of the weaponry creating a low pressure zone at the top of the unit, siphoning heat away from the components and requiring no other active cooling. That overclocking algorithm using the increased compute overhead to constantly monitor the status of the components and feather the voltage?''\n\n''What about it all?''\n\n''This is a piece of art, man. You really gotta start giving yourself some credit.''\n\n\n<style=cMono>//-- Transcriptions complete. --//</style></style>",
		"TURRETLING_DT_LORE": "<style=cSub><style=cMono>//-- ERROR\n//-- MECHANICAL OBSTRUCTION: LEG SEGMENT 11\n//-- AWAITING MANUAL INTERVENTION</style>\n\n''What's wrong, you get something stuck in your gears, Scuttle? Let's see what you've got jammed in there...''\n\n \n\n''A beetle leg? And a big one, too! You must've had a lot of trouble getting back with that weighing you down. \n\n... There. All free. Good job, Scutt.''\n\n<style=cMono>\n//-- IMPACT DETECTED\n//-- LOCATION: TURRET BATTERY\n//-- FORCE OF IMPACT: 15N\n//-- DETECTING INTENT... PRAISE DETECTED\n//-- :)\n//-- ENTERING STANDBY --//</style></style>",
		"TURRETLING_DTDEMO_LORE": "<style=cSub><style=cMono>//-- INITIALIZING --\n//-- BEGINNING SYSTEMS TESTS --\n//-- FIRMWARE ERROR --\n//-- ATTEMPTING REFLASH --\n//-- FIRMWARE ERROR --\n//-- USER INPUT REQUIRED --//</style>\n\n''Alright, just need to flash the new version on so you can actually see all your new hardware...''\n\n<style=cMono>//-- INPUT ACCEPTED --\n//-- BIOS REFLASH SUCCESSFUL --\n//-- GOOD MORNING, OPERATOR --//</style>\n\n''Good morning, Scott! You've gotten some upgrades over the last version. Let's get all that running.''\n\n<style=cStack>>> INCOMING COMMAND...\n>> SUDO INIT ARM_NOOBTB.CMD -o -c\n\n> OK. WARMING ARMAMENT...\n> ACQUIRING TARGET... FOUND.\n> ARMAMENT OPERATION: INITIATED.\n> AMMUNITION: 5 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:00>\n> TARGET EFFECT... INCONCLUSIVE.\n> AMMUNITION: 4 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:03\n> TARGET EFFECT... INCONCLUSIVE.\n> AMMUNITION: 3 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:06\n> TARGET EFFECT... INCONCLUSIVE.\n> AMMUNITION: 2 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:09\n> TARGET EFFECT... INCONCLUSIVE.\n> AMMUNITION: 1 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:12\n> TARGET EFFECT... INCONCLUSIVE.\n> AMMUNITION: 0 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:15\n> ARMAMENT DEPLETED.\n> TARGET EFFECT... CONFIRMED.\n\n> PLEASE ENTER COMMAND_</style>\n\n''Let's... rework those targeting parameters, and try again.''\n\n<style=cMono>//-- COMMLINK TERMINATED --//\n//-- BEGIN HIBERNATION --//</style></style>",
		"TURRETLING_ARTI_LORE": "<style=cSub><style=cMono>//-- AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM CREW QUARTERS OF UES [Redacted] --//</style>\n\n\n''They're crazy popular.''\n\n''What do you MEAN they're crazy popular? They're an autonomous fleet of KILLING MACHINES! Why does the High Court woman have one of my turrets dressed up in her colors, relaxing in a SHRINE in her quarters?''\n\n''She likes the little guy. She's not the only one, either''\n\n''Is this going to be better or worse for my health if I'm informed as to what you cretins are doing to MY HARDWARE?''\n\n''Well, I repaired one that landed funny down planet-side. You made them pretty easy to fix, thanks for that. Cap's got one that hangs out on his desk. He calls it 'Paperweight' but he gives it little pets and chirps when he thinks there ain't anybody looking. Few others 'round the ship got the same idea, what with your fleet of killing machines wandering the place.''\n\n''I can't believe this. Do you have ANY idea how many hours I spent on planning those units' schematics, let alone all the time fabricating and DEBUGGING? YEARS of my life on this project, all to field unmanned excursions down to the planet. Now the crew are ADOPTING them, like a litter of kittens!''\n\n''Yeah, pretty much.''\n\n''I hate this.''\n\n''Well, too bad. Ain't our fault you made 'em so cute.''\n\n<style=cMono>\n//-- Transcriptions complete. --//</style></style>",
		"SWARMLING_LORE": "<style=cSub><style=cMono>//-- AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM CREW QUARTERS OF UES [Redacted] --//</style>\n\n\n''Whaddaya got there? A game?''\n\n''A GAME?! Buzz off, I'm doing fieldwork. IMPORTANT fieldwork!''\n\n''Looks like something one of the keyboard jockeys plays during breaks to me... Plays it on shift too, if nothing needs monitoring.''\n\n''Consider paying even the SLIGHEST bit of attention to what's going on past the tip of your nose, eh? Anything look familiar? Like say, that curved pillar? Or that stone platform?''\n\n''Oh... Yeah. You're piloting those things down on the planet?''\n\n''Eureka! She finally gets it! \n\nYes it's a networked swarm of my custom CT-CHB Mobile Walker Turret. Piloted via my custom software using the ship's comms array, allowing for sub-5 millisecond input latency from low orbit down to the planet's surface. Even works up to a thousand meters below. I say 'shoot' from up here, and they shoot before you could even blink.\n\nA complete upgrade over those ancient TC-2RT junkers you see dotted around down there from the Contact Light. Miniaturized frame offering no drawbacks to the older model in terms of structural integrity, and a massively elevating the model's threat pacification capabilities. Now with ambulatory limbs capable of traversal comparable to meat-sacks like us, and it packs flat for easy storage, transport, and repair.''\n\n''All of them?''\n\n''What do you mean, 'all of them'? The majority of the fleet is the miniaturized model, while others have some... custom hardware. Purely for specialized operational parameters, of course.''\n\n''No, like... You're controlling all of them? I've seen a whole bunch of those things laying around. Even patched one up for myself. Pretty slick that you can handle all that with just the two hands.''\n\n''NO, you meathe-\n\nNo, they have autonomous protocols when manually activated by anyone planet-side. I'm only one-... well, most of one man, but things still need doing down there. The CT-CHB swarm can become my eyes and gun barrels on the planet, even beyond the limitations of this singular body.''\n\n''What's up with that one glowing rainbow colors?''\n\n''Ah, yes, the overdrive protocol. Naturally, some situations may require more force than any individual unit can exert at a given time. So, I've designed a special subroutine to run that allows for limited-time overclocking right up against their failure thresholds, vastly augmenting their capabilities. Thus far, I've run into... difficulties getting the subroutine to run correctly under autonomous function. As an 'Emergency' command, it can't be run remotely. Therefore, the subroutine occurs randomly on the units you'll find planet-side. For now, just consider it a bit of good luck if you happen upon a Rainbowized unit.''\n\n''Okay. That really doesn't explain the rainbow colors.''\n\n''The... um, excessive voltage running through the modules causes their indicator lighting and thermochromic hull panels to... temporarily malfunction. A technical glitch, is all.''\n\n''Sure. Now, that one's bright orange. All the other ones are neon or pastel colors too. I even remember seeing one with some bunny ears and a slice of cake sat on it. Just what kind of 'specialized operational parameters' need bunny ears?''\n\n''...''\n\n''Look, you can just say you wanted them to look cute. Ain't no shame in it.''\n\n''I-\n\n...\n\nYou will not speak a word of this to ANYONE.''\n\n''You got it, boss.''\n\n\n<style=cMono>//-- Transcriptions complete. --//</style></style>",
	}
}